# Method for Producing a Pre-Insulated Pipe

A method for manufacturing a pre-insulated pipe, comprising the following steps:

Inserting a length of jacket pipe (10) into a guide channel (110) defined by a front end (111) and a rear end (112);

Securing said length of jacket pipe (10) within said guide channel (110);

Providing a first end (21) of a length of insulated inner piping (20), wherein said length of insulated inner piping comprises an inner pipe surrounded by at least one layer of compressible insulation material (26);

Introducing, at the front end of said guide channel, said first end of the length of insulated inner piping (20) into said length of jacket pipe (10);

Applying an overpressure at least within the interior of said length of jacket pipe (10), surrounding the inserted first end of the length of insulated inner piping (20);

Advancing said first end of the length of insulated inner piping (20) toward the rear end of said guide channel (110), wherein said overpressure is sufficient to radially compress said at least one layer of insulation material (26); and

Releasing said overpressure to secure the length of insulated inner piping (20) within the length of jacket pipe (10), thereby forming the pre-insulated pipe.

